/* bat_anom_model.h - unsupervised battery anomaly detector parameters (generated by gen_p3.py).
 * Struct layout = an_params_t in bat_anom_core.h (the reference: anom_host.c, ref_anom.py). Window 60 s, warm-up 24 h, alarm after 3 consecutive windows.
 * Features: innov_mean, innov_rms, rest_dvdt_Vph, rest_current_C, thermal_resid_C, r_sag_ratio, r_step_ratio, dis_load_C, glitches.
 * Held-out benign false alarms (Raw blocks, 388 h): autoencoder 0.0026/h (95 % upper 0.012),
 * robust z 0.245/h, Gaussian 0.126/h. Only the autoencoder passes the 0.05/h gate, so
 * BAT_ANOM_ALARM_MASK keeps only its bit for the user-facing warning; the other two are logged as diagnostics.
 * Thresholds were calibrated on Raw_data lab cycling and MUST be re-learned from the board's own warm-up.
 * The OS decides the action (banner, log, load shedding); the detector never cuts power.
 */
